code: K0032
title: Style Error
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, style, set-rule, ui-element]
description: "'set' style rule is malformed or placed in an invalid scope"
---

A `set` style rule (`set target(prop: value, ...)`) is malformed or placed in an invalid position. Each `set` rule must target a valid element name followed by parenthesized style arguments, and `set view(...)` may only appear at the top level of a file or directly before the body of a `view` function.

## Example

This error occurs when a `set` rule is missing its target name or argument list, or when `set view(...)` is placed inside a nested block or non-view helper:

```kura
set (fill: black)

fn helper() => {
  set view(fill: white)
  #text("Invalid placement")
}
```

## Solution

Specify a valid element name and parenthesized property arguments, and place `set view(...)` only at the top level or immediately before a `view` body:

```kura
set button(fill: black)

fn view() =>
  set view(fill: white)
  #button("Click me")
```
